# SRG-APP-000172-WSR-000104  -  CAT I
# The web server must encrypt passwords during transmission.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000172-WSR-000104
group:           V-206387
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000197
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk Web can be configured to serve only over TLS with a named
                 certificate and private key, and the alternate GET-based login endpoint
                 that would carry a password in a URL can be left disabled, so credentials
                 never cross the network in the clear.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] serverCert non_empty
check:           web.conf [settings] privKeyPath non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enable_insecure_login https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] privKeyPath https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] serverCert https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] enable_insecure_login equals false
                 reason: "Whether or not the GET-based '/account/insecurelogin' REST
                         endpoint is enabled. Provides an alternate GET-based authentication
                         mechanism. If 'true', the following url is available:
                         http://localhost:8000/en-US/account/insecurelogin?loginType=splunk&username=noc&password=XXXXXXX.
                         If 'false', only the main /account/login endpoint is available.
                         Default: false"
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Any reverse proxy or load balancer in front of Splunk Web must not
                 terminate TLS and forward credentials in the clear; that configuration
                 lives in the proxy, not in Splunk
external:        Whether the named certificate was issued by an approved certificate
                 authority
external:        Password transmission to an LDAP or SAML provider is additionally governed
                 by that provider's connection settings, including the OpenLDAP client
                 configuration named in SPLK-CL-000320

citation:        SPLK-CL-000330 check and fix text (enableSplunkWebSSL = 1 with privKeyPath
                 and serverCert); web.conf.spec:70-73 (enableSplunkWebSSL, default false),
                 web.conf.spec:75-91 (privKeyPath and serverCert), web.conf.spec:198-205
                 (enable_insecure_login, default false; when true the GET
                 /account/insecurelogin endpoint accepts a password in the URL)
finding:         web.conf [settings] does not enable TLS for Splunk Web with a named
                 certificate and private key, or enable_insecure_login is true, so the
                 application transmits account passwords without encryption or exposes them
                 in a request URL.
